// End-to-end example schema for issue #306 (epic #298's last story): a
// small "task board" — two models with a real relation, plus one
// procedure — rich enough to exercise the `swr` layout's full surface
// (list/get/create/update/delete hooks, invalidation, a query
// procedure) without tripping either of the layout's two known
// pre-existing gaps: no `@@paged` model here (the layout never imports
// `Page`/`PageInfo` for one — see the generator's own follow-up ticket),
// and no two model names that collapse under `to_camel_case` (the
// default layout's `cratestack QueryKeys` collision — irrelevant to
// `swr`'s own key factory, which nests under each model's literal
// route instead, but avoided here anyway since it costs nothing).
//
// `transport rest` (the default — no `transport rpc` line) keeps the
// wire format plain `fetch`/JSON, the simplest shape for a first real
// consumer of `--swr` to read end to end.
//
// The schema is split across files with `part` (cratestack#924): this root
// holds the `datasource` and `auth` blocks, and `schema/` holds one part per
// concern (the two models, then the procedures and their types). The split
// changes nothing downstream: the macro, the generated Rust, Dart and
// TypeScript clients, and `SCHEMA_SHA256` are identical to the single-file
// schema's (`tests/schema_identity.rs`, `just regen-examples --check`).

datasource db {
  provider = "postgresql"
  url = env("DATABASE_URL")
}

auth Caller {
  id Int
}

part "schema/board.cstack"
part "schema/task.cstack"
part "schema/procedures.cstack"
